    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` to the v2 export API.\n\nChanges:\n- Calls `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `/v1/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` until `drained` is `true`, rather than assuming one response contains everything.\n- Deduplicates on payout `id`, since adjacent windows overlap by one payout.\n- Retries `429` responses after the `Retry-After` delay, re-sending the identical request/cursor.\n- Restarts the export from the beginning on `400 invalid_cursor`, relying on id deduplication to remain exactly-once.\n\nVerification against the live v2 server at `http://the VM's public address:18080`:\n- Synced **2,431** payouts.\n- all **2,431** ids were unique.\n- No payouts missing or extra compared with v1.\n- Output order matched v1 exactly.\n- The run exercised real `429` handling successfully.\n\nAlso tested locally with a mock v2 server covering overlapping windows, `429` retries, and invalid-cursor restart; all produced the correct 7 unique payouts.",
